course: dictionary
lesson: 13492
title: Words you cannot read
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Illegible is a long word, but its clues are easy to find. The start il- often means not, as in impossible or unkind, so illegible means not legible. Legible means clear enough to read.
explain: «Jack's handwriting was so messy that his teacher could not read a single word of it.» The words messy and could not read tell you that illegible means too unclear to be read. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «The sign above the shop had faded in the sun, and the letters were almost illegible.» Faded and almost show that the letters are hard to see. Illegible is about writing, signs or notes that are too unclear to read.
fact: Illegible means too messy, faded or unclear to be read.
fact: The prefix il- means not, so illegible means not legible.
fact: Illegible can describe handwriting, faded signs or smudged notes.
fact: «Almost illegible» means you can only just make out some of the words.
fact: The opposite of illegible is legible, which means clear enough to read.
exercise: «The note from the teacher was illegible, so Sam could not read his homework.» What does illegible mean? | *Too messy to be read | Written in gold ink | Very long and full of pictures
exercise: «The faded street sign was illegible, so we could not tell which road to take.» Find and copy one word that means not able to be read. | *illegible | road | faded | street
exercise: Mum says, «Your shopping list is almost illegible.» What does almost illegible tell you? | The list has been eaten | The list is written in another language | The list is perfectly clear | *You can only just make out the words
test: «The rain had washed the chalk off the board, leaving illegible scribbles.» What are the scribbles like? | Pictures of animals and trees | Perfectly neat writing | *Too faded or messy to be read
test: Which word means the opposite of illegible? | *legible | unlikely | illegal | invisible
exam: «The doctor's prescription was so illegible that the chemist had to phone to check.» What does illegible mean here? | Very cheap | Written in red ink | Full of pictures of doctors | *Too unclear to be read
